WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.050
Ammonia is made by joining
nitrogen and hydrogen,

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.550
in huge plants that run day and night.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.790
Run the reaction cooler,

4
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.030
and the mixture ends up
holding more ammonia.

5
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.150
Yet every ammonia plant deliberately
runs much hotter than that.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.310
So why would engineers choose
conditions that give less product?

7
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.710
In this mission, you'll meet a
reversible reaction that never

8
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:23.780
quite finishes.

9
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.370
You'll see how changing the
temperature and the pressure pushes

10
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.570
the equilibrium one way or the other.

11
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.130
Then you'll weigh up the
yield, the speed and the cost,

12
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.490
to find out how the real
conditions are chosen.

13
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.420
Your mission: explain why
ammonia plants run hot.
